;; spec:   stdlib §2.5 (a bulk vec builds the trie in one pass), §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 2080
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 138
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; vec-from-array (L9) of 2080 elements: 64 full leaves, which is exactly two groups of 32 for the level
;; above (and a tail of 32). A group count rounded up one too far (the number of groups
;; of 64 leaves computed as 3 and not 2) builds a third, empty branch that the next level then drops
;; unread, so every element still reads right and only the count shows it (3 objects more: 141). The mutation
;; review (MUT-L9) found `(+ n 31)` to `(+ n 32)` in the group count surviving every case before this one;
;; the two differ exactly when the leaf count is a multiple of 32 above 32. 138 is measured; the
;; harness's own test lowers the bound by one and requires the failure.
(ns main)

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec-from-array (array 2080 0))))
    (vec-count v)))
